## Common Pitfalls to Avoid

1. ❌ Using relative imports in Python backend
2. ❌ Using Python 3.13 (compatibility issues)
3. ❌ Not handling database sessions properly
4. ❌ Using 'use client' unnecessarily in Next.js
5. ❌ Not validating user inputs
6. ❌ Exposing sensitive data in error messages
7. ❌ Not testing code before committing
8. ❌ Creating classes when functions suffice
9. ❌ Not handling async operations properly
10. ❌ Ignoring TypeScript errors

